PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769653188
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, An appeal by six Irishmen against their
OL,6, convictions for the 1974 Birmingham pub
OL,7, bombings has been rejected.
OL,9,FLord Chief Justice Lord Lane, sitting
OL,10,Fwith two appeal judges, gave judgement
OL,11,Fon the appeal - ordered by the Home
OL,12,FSecretary - at the Old Bailey.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FLord Gifford, for the six men, said
OL,15,Fthey would be seeking leave to appeal
OL,16,Fto the House of Lords.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe men, Patrick Hill, Hugh Callaghan,
OL,19,FJohnny Walker, Richard McIlkenny, Gerry
OL,20,FHunter and Billy Power were jailed for
OL,21,Flife for the bombings in which 21
OL,22,Fpeople died.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 28-01-88
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769653188
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, At the Old Bailey appeal hearing of six
OL,6, Irishmen convicted of the Birmingham
OL,7, pub bombing in 1974, three main sources
OL,8, of fresh evidence were rejected.
OL,10,FThe three appeal judges said evidence
OL,11,Ffrom a cleaner, of blood on cell walls,
OL,12,Fwas unsupported by any other evidence.
OL,14,FAdditionally they did not believe a
OL,15,Fwoman police officer, who had told the
OL,16,Fcourt of violence in police cells.
OL,18,FThey also said a former policeman, who
OL,19,Ftold the appeal police had ill-treated
OL,20,Fthe six, wanted only to blacken the
OL,21,Fname of the West Midlands police.
OL,23,T]CFrom 28-01-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769653188
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The convictions of six Irishmen for the
OL,6, 1974 Birmingham pub bombings were safe
OL,7, and satisfactory, the Lord Chief
OL,8, Justice Lord Lane told the Appeal Court
OL,10,FGiving judgement, Lord Lane, sitting
OL,11,Fwith two other judges, said the longer
OL,12,Fthe hearings had gone on the more
OL,13,Fconvinced they were that the verdicts
OL,14,Fwere right.
OL,16,FEarlier, he had ruled out the
OL,17,Fpossibility of a re-trial.
OL,19,FIt would be unjust for the six to be
OL,20,Ftried again after 13 years, he said.
OL,21,FThere was no halfway house, if there
OL,22,Fwas doubt the appeal must be allowed.
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 28-01-88
