OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, More than half of television viewers
OL,6, think programmes contain too much
OL,7, violence, says a study published today.
OL,9,FThe publication of the study follows
OL,10,Fa decision by Independent Broadcasting
OL,11,FAuthority members since the Hungerford
OL,12,Fmassacre that peak-time TV violence
OL,13,Fshould be cut.
OL,15,FBut the IBA survey also shows that
OL,16,Fspecific crime shows like The A-Team
OL,17,Fare not thought harmful to chldren.
OL,19,FAbout 90 per cent of viewers also
OL,20,Fthought parents should take more care
OL,21,Fover what their children watched.
OL,23,T]CFrom 28-01-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
