PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769653188
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/24
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Top East German physicist and former
OL,6, spy Mr Klaus Fuchs has died aged 76.
OL,8,FMr Fuchs helped build the first nuclear
OL,9,Fbomb but was best known in the West for
OL,10,Fspying while working at Birmingham
OL,11,FUniversity.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FHe served nine years of his 14-year
OL,14,Fprison sentence before returning to
OL,15,Fhis country in 1959, where he continued
OL,16,Fhis work in nuclear research.
OL,18,FMr Fuchs retired from East Germany's
OL,19,Finstitute of atomic affairs as its
OL,20,Fdeputy head in 1979.
OL,21,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 28-01-88 / teletextarchive.com
